UID:kasos-holocaust-of-kasos-commemoration-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270607
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270608
SUMMARY:Holocaust of Kasos commemoration
LOCATION:Kasos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Memorial of the 1824 destruction of the island by Egyptian-Ottoman forces. Solemn\, not festive — but historically the most important date in the Kasos calendar.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kasos/#holocaust-of-kasos-commemoration
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kasos/#holocaust-of-kasos-commemoration
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:sifnos-chrysopigi-near-platys-gialos-panigiri-of-panagia-chrysopigi-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270609
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270611
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia Chrysopigi (Ascension)\, Chrysopigi
LOCATION:Chrysopigi (near Platys Gialos)\, Sifnos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Sifnos's biggest festival\, at the cliff-top monastery. The icon is paraded\; tavernas serve free chickpea stew and lamb to all comers.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/sifnos/#chrysopigi-near-platys-gialos-panigiri-of-panagia-chrysopigi
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/sifnos/#chrysopigi-near-platys-gialos-panigiri-of-panagia-chrysopigi
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kea-ioulida-pentecost-panigiri-ioulida-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270619
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270621
SUMMARY:Pentecost panigiri\, Ioulida
LOCATION:Ioulida\, Kea (Tzia)\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The municipality's 'traditional Agiou Pnevmatos panigiri' in Ioulida on the evening of Pentecost Sunday from 21:00 — an island glenti in the main square with live violin and laouto and Tziotiko dancing\, the first big night of the Kea summer. It coincides with the three-day Pentecost weekend when Athenians pour onto the island\, so book the Lavrio ferry and your room well ahead.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kea/#ioulida-pentecost-panigiri-ioulida
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kea/#ioulida-pentecost-panigiri-ioulida
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ikaria-negia-panigiri-of-agia-triada-pentecost-negia-kionio-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270620
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270621
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Triada (Pentecost)\, Negia (Kionio)
LOCATION:Negia\, Ikaria\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The early-season panigiri on the Agios Kirykos side: on Pentecost Sunday the tiny settlement of Negia (Kionio) near Agios Kirykos keeps Agia Triada with a traditional Ikarian feast after the liturgy. Negia also has a small panigiri for Prophet Zechariah on 5 September. Kastanies (Tragostasi) in Raches keeps Agiou Pnevmatos the following day.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#negia-panigiri-of-agia-triada-pentecost-negia-kionio
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#negia-panigiri-of-agia-triada-pentecost-negia-kionio
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kythnos-chora-messaria-panigiri-of-agia-triada-chora-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270620
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270622
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Triada\, Chora
LOCATION:Chora (Messaria)\, Kythnos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:One of the two feasts Kythnos itself names as its most important: Agia Triada in Chora\, on the eve and day of Agiou Pnevmatos (Whit Monday). The pattern is the island's classic — vespers\, then an all-night glenti with local violin and laouto players and the Kythnian 'balos' dance in the square\, continuing after the morning liturgy. Chora is a 10-minute drive from Merichas\; the square fills\, so come at dusk.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kythnos/#chora-messaria-panigiri-of-agia-triada-chora
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kythnos/#chora-messaria-panigiri-of-agia-triada-chora
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:lasithi-palaikastro-panigiri-of-agia-triada-pentecost-palaikastro-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270620
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270621
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Triada (Pentecost)\, Palaikastro
LOCATION:Palaikastro\, Crete (Lasithi)\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The first big panigiri of the Sitia summer: on Pentecost Sunday evening the Palaikastro association sets tables in the schoolyard with a full menu (about 18 euros in 2025) and top Cretan musicians (Antonis and Nikos Xylouris in 2025). Palaikastro is the base for Vai and Kouremenos beaches\, so it fits a June stay\; book a table through the association.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lasithi/#palaikastro-panigiri-of-agia-triada-pentecost-palaikastro
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lasithi/#palaikastro-panigiri-of-agia-triada-pentecost-palaikastro
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:lesvos-bull-sacrifice-tavros-of-saint-charalambos-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270620
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270621
SUMMARY:Bull sacrifice (Tavros) of Saint Charalambos
LOCATION:Lesvos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:In Agia Paraskevi village\, an ancient and unusual ritual: a bull is paraded\, blessed\, then ritually slaughtered and shared communally. Pre-Christian roots\, controversial in modern times\, but among Greece's most extraordinary surviving folk traditions.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lesvos/#bull-sacrifice-tavros-of-saint-charalambos
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lesvos/#bull-sacrifice-tavros-of-saint-charalambos
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:milos-adamas-panigiri-of-agia-triada-adamas-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270620
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270622
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Triada\, Adamas
LOCATION:Adamas\, Milos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The port town's big feast: vespers at Agia Triada on Pentecost Sunday evening\, a procession of the icon along the Adamas waterfront\, then from about 21:30 an island glenti with live violin and lute\, dancing by the local KAPI dance group and food on the church forecourt\; liturgy follows on Whit Monday morning. It's a short walk from any hotel in Adamas\, so no car needed — just arrive by 21:00 for a seat.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/milos/#adamas-panigiri-of-agia-triada-adamas
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/milos/#adamas-panigiri-of-agia-triada-adamas
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:naxos-filoti-panigiri-of-agia-triada-holy-spirit-monday-filoti-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270620
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270622
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Triada (Holy Spirit Monday)\, Filoti
LOCATION:Filoti\, Naxos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Filoti's early-summer feast at the church of Agia Triada\, on Holy Spirit Monday: violins and laouta in the square\, food and wine and dancing until the early hours. A quieter preview of what the village does on 15 August.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/naxos/#filoti-panigiri-of-agia-triada-holy-spirit-monday-filoti
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/naxos/#filoti-panigiri-of-agia-triada-holy-spirit-monday-filoti
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nisyros-mandraki-panigiri-of-agios-nikitas-patron-mandraki-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270620
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270622
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Nikitas (patron)\, Mandraki
LOCATION:Mandraki\, Nisyros\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The island's patron saint is celebrated in Mandraki on 20-21 June with a procession of the icon through the village and a glendi. It opens the summer season of panigiria on Nisyros.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/nisyros/#mandraki-panigiri-of-agios-nikitas-patron-mandraki
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/nisyros/#mandraki-panigiri-of-agios-nikitas-patron-mandraki
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:othonoi-ammos-othonoi-feast-of-the-holy-spirit-agiou-pnevmatos-othon-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270621
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270622
SUMMARY:Feast of the Holy Spirit (Agiou Pnevmatos)\, Othonoi
LOCATION:Ammos\, Othonoi\, Othonoi\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The Monday after Pentecost is the day the Corfu festival calendars give for Othonoi\, the westernmost point of Greece: liturgy\, then a village meal and music by the harbour at Ammos for the islanders and the first summer visitors. The ferry from Agios Stefanos (Corfu) is the only way\; it runs a few times a week in June\, so plan to stay a night.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/othonoi/#ammos-othonoi-feast-of-the-holy-spirit-agiou-pnevmatos-othon
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/othonoi/#ammos-othonoi-feast-of-the-holy-spirit-agiou-pnevmatos-othon
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:amorgos-chora-klidonas-midsummer-feast-chora-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270623
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270625
SUMMARY:Klidonas midsummer feast\, Chora
LOCATION:Chora\, Amorgos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On 23 June from about 20:30 the municipality and the Chora associations light the Klidonas fire in the Loza square\, with the fortune-telling custom\, traditional music and dancing. A short\, friendly evening and the opening of Amorgos's summer.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/amorgos/#chora-klidonas-midsummer-feast-chora
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/amorgos/#chora-klidonas-midsummer-feast-chora
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:antiparos-antiparos-chora-klidonas-bonfires-of-agios-ioannis-antiparos-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270623
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270625
SUMMARY:Klidonas bonfires of Agios Ioannis\, Antiparos harbour
LOCATION:Antiparos (Chora)\, Antiparos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On the evening of 23 June the May wreaths from the doorways are collected and burned on the waterfront\, children jump the fires and the local dance group performs the Klidonas custom\, with kerasmata and music afterwards. Small and genuinely local\; it is over by midnight.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/antiparos/#antiparos-chora-klidonas-bonfires-of-agios-ioannis-antiparos
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/antiparos/#antiparos-chora-klidonas-bonfires-of-agios-ioannis-antiparos
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:evia-north-limni-klidonas-of-ai-giannis-limni-harbour-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270623
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270625
SUMMARY:Klidonas of Ai-Giannis\, Limni harbour
LOCATION:Limni\, Evia (North)\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On 23 June the Elymnians light the St John's bonfire on the harbour of Limni and revive the klidonas: girls' tokens drawn from a jug of 'silent water'\, couplets\, jumping the flames\, then music on the quay. It is in the municipal summer programme every year and free\; the seafront tavernas are the place to sit and watch.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/evia-north/#limni-klidonas-of-ai-giannis-limni-harbour
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/evia-north/#limni-klidonas-of-ai-giannis-limni-harbour
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:heraklion-houdetsi-klidonas-houdetsi-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270623
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270625
SUMMARY:Klidonas\, Houdetsi
LOCATION:Houdetsi\, Crete (Heraklion)\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The Peza wine village revives the St John's Eve custom properly: on the afternoon of 23 June the May wreaths are burned and people jump the bonfire three times\, the 'silent water' is fetched and the girls' fortunes read\, then Cretan music in the square with free entry (Kakoudakis and Petsakis in 2025). Houdetsi is 20 km south of Heraklion\; the Erotokritos cultural workshop organises it.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/heraklion/#houdetsi-klidonas-houdetsi
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/heraklion/#houdetsi-klidonas-houdetsi
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ios-pyrgos-agios-ioannis-monastery-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-kli-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270623
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270625
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Ioannis (Klidonas) at Pyrgos monastery
LOCATION:Pyrgos (Agios Ioannis monastery)\, Ios\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On the evening of 23 June Ios climbs to the little monastery of Agios Ioannis at Pyrgos\, on the summit above Chora\, for the Klidonas: vespers\, then bonfires\, meze and wine from the association and violins until late\, with the whole island laid out beneath you. Take the dirt road by car and walk the last stretch\, or hike up from Chora before dusk.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ios/#pyrgos-agios-ioannis-monastery-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-kli
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ios/#pyrgos-agios-ioannis-monastery-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-kli
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kalymnos-pothia-and-beaches-klidonas-bonfires-of-agios-ioannis-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270623
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270625
SUMMARY:Klidonas bonfires of Agios Ioannis
LOCATION:Pothia and beaches\, Kalymnos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On the evening of 23 June small bonfires are lit on the beaches and along the harbours of Kalymnos and children and teenagers jump over them for the Klidonas\, the midsummer custom of Agios Ioannis. Nothing organised\, just wander the Pothia waterfront or Myrties beach after dark.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kalymnos/#pothia-and-beaches-klidonas-bonfires-of-agios-ioannis
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kalymnos/#pothia-and-beaches-klidonas-bonfires-of-agios-ioannis
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kea-otzias-klidonas-custom-otzias-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270623
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270625
SUMMARY:Klidonas custom\, Otzias
LOCATION:Otzias\, Kea (Tzia)\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On the evening of 23 June the Otzias beautification society and the women's association revive the Klidonas at the beach village of Otzias\, from 20:00: the 'silent water'\, the reading of fortunes from the pot\, bonfires that people jump over\, and music and dancing afterwards. It's a family-oriented evening rather than a big panigiri\; there is easy parking along the bay.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kea/#otzias-klidonas-custom-otzias
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kea/#otzias-klidonas-custom-otzias
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:lefkada-pinakochori-lamparda-of-agios-ioannis-fire-jumping-pinakocho-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270623
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270625
SUMMARY:Lamparda of Agios Ioannis (fire-jumping)\, Pinakochori
LOCATION:Pinakochori\, Lefkada\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On the eve of St John's day the Sfakiotes village of Pinakochori lights big bonfires ('lamparda') of last year's dried oregano in the old school yard after evening service\, and everyone jumps over the flames three times for luck\, then there is music and dancing. It is the only Sfakiotes village that kept the custom\; organised by the Sfakiotes cultural centre since 1990\, low-key and very local.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lefkada/#pinakochori-lamparda-of-agios-ioannis-fire-jumping-pinakocho
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lefkada/#pinakochori-lamparda-of-agios-ioannis-fire-jumping-pinakocho
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:paros-naoussa-klidonas-bonfires-of-agios-ioannis-naoussa-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270623
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270625
SUMMARY:Klidonas bonfires of Agios Ioannis\, Naoussa
LOCATION:Naoussa\, Paros\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On the evening of 23 June the harbour of Naoussa (and\, smaller\, Aliki and Prodromos) lights the Klidonas bonfires: the dried May wreaths go on the fire\, kids and the local dance group jump over it\, and the cultural association hands out meze and wine with violin and laouto. It is a short\, early-summer event rather than an all-nighter\, so turn up around 21:00 and stay for the dancing on the quay.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/paros/#naoussa-klidonas-bonfires-of-agios-ioannis-naoussa
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/paros/#naoussa-klidonas-bonfires-of-agios-ioannis-naoussa
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:poros-poros-town-klidonas-of-ai-giannis-poros-town-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270623
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270625
SUMMARY:Klidonas of Ai-Giannis\, Poros Town
LOCATION:Poros Town\, Poros\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On the night of 23 June the neighbourhoods of Poros town light St John's fires and jump them\, with mezes\, music and dancing in the lanes below the clock tower. Informal and free\; the seafront is the place to see the fires from.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/poros/#poros-town-klidonas-of-ai-giannis-poros-town
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/poros/#poros-town-klidonas-of-ai-giannis-poros-town
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:skiathos-skiathos-town-klidonas-bonfires-of-ai-giannis-skiathos-town-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270623
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270625
SUMMARY:Klidonas bonfires of Ai-Giannis\, Skiathos Town
LOCATION:Skiathos Town\, Skiathos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On the evening of 23 June the old neighbourhoods of the Chora (Plakes\, Agios Nikolaos\, around the church of Ai-Giannis) light bonfires\, burn the May Day wreaths and children jump the flames three times for luck. There is violin-and-lute music\, teasing couplets\, oregano (the saint is 'Riganas' here) and wine poured for anyone standing nearby. It is a neighbourhood custom\, not a ticketed event\, so just walk up from the old port after 9 pm and follow the smoke.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/skiathos/#skiathos-town-klidonas-bonfires-of-ai-giannis-skiathos-town
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/skiathos/#skiathos-town-klidonas-bonfires-of-ai-giannis-skiathos-town
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:skopelos-kampos-skopelos-town-vigil-of-agios-ioannis-prodromos-kampos-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270623
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270625
SUMMARY:Vigil of Agios Ioannis Prodromos\, Kampos (Skopelos)
LOCATION:Kampos (Skopelos Town)\, Skopelos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The small women's monastery of Prodromos a few km from the Chora keeps an all-night vigil on the eve of 24 June and offers food to those who stay\, in the Athonite manner the island's monasteries follow. The same dependency's chapel of Agios Ioannis sto Kampo (not the Mamma Mia rock chapel at Kastri) holds vespers on 28 August and liturgy on the 29th for the Beheading. Quiet\, candle-lit and worth it if you are on the island anyway\; take a car\, there is no bus.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/skopelos/#kampos-skopelos-town-vigil-of-agios-ioannis-prodromos-kampos
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/skopelos/#kampos-skopelos-town-vigil-of-agios-ioannis-prodromos-kampos
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:syros-chroussa-klidonas-bonfires-chroussa-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270623
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270625
SUMMARY:Klidonas bonfires\, Chroussa
LOCATION:Chroussa\, Syros\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The village of Chroussa in the south of Syros revives the Klidonas on the night of 23-24 June at the old Faneromeni primary school: the May wreaths are burned\, kids jump the fire\, and the association serves meze and wine with live music. Small and local\; 20 minutes by car from Ermoupoli.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/syros/#chroussa-klidonas-bonfires-chroussa
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/syros/#chroussa-klidonas-bonfires-chroussa
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:thasos-limenas-fires-of-st-john-klidonas-limenas-skala-marion-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270623
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270625
SUMMARY:Fires of St John (Klidonas)\, Limenas & Skala Marion
LOCATION:Limenas\, Thasos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On the eve of St John (23 June) Limenas park hosts the 'Fires of Ai-Giannis': the Klidonas divination custom\, choir\, jumping the bonfire and halva handed round. Skala Marion on the west coast keeps the same feast on 23-24 June with an icon procession and a village celebration. First real village events of the Thasos summer.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/thasos/#limenas-fires-of-st-john-klidonas-limenas-skala-marion
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/thasos/#limenas-fires-of-st-john-klidonas-limenas-skala-marion
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:milos-klidonas-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270624
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270625
SUMMARY:Klidonas
LOCATION:Milos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Folk Saint John's Eve tradition still alive on Milos: at sunset\, unmarried girls collect water from a well in silence and predict their future husbands through tokens placed in it overnight. Bonfires are jumped on the 24th. Smaller and more intimate than the better-known Cretan version.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/milos/#klidonas
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/milos/#klidonas
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:spetses-agioi-pantes-above-agia-marina-feast-of-agioi-pantes-monaste-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270626
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270628
SUMMARY:Feast of Agioi Pantes Monastery (All Saints Sunday)
LOCATION:Agioi Pantes (above Agia Marina)\, Spetses\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The women's monastery of Agioi Pantes\, 1.5 km up a cypress avenue from Agios Eleftherios with a view over Agia Marina bay\, keeps All Saints Sunday (the Sunday after Pentecost) with a vigil and a liturgy\, after which the nuns serve coffee and sweets in the courtyard. Early June\, before the crowds\; walk up in the morning.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/spetses/#agioi-pantes-above-agia-marina-feast-of-agioi-pantes-monaste
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/spetses/#agioi-pantes-above-agia-marina-feast-of-agioi-pantes-monaste
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kythnos-dryopida-panigiri-of-agioi-apostoloi-dryopida-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270628
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270630
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agioi Apostoloi\, Dryopida
LOCATION:Dryopida\, Kythnos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The feast of the Metropolitan church of Peter and Paul in Dryopida is the village's biggest night and an official municipal event: hierarchical vespers at 19:30 on 28 June\, then from 21:00 a traditional glenti with violins in the square with the Dryopida Cultural Society's dance groups\, and liturgy at 07:30 on the 29th. Dryopida's tiled-roof lanes are pedestrian\; traffic is closed on the approach road\, so park at the edge of the village and walk in.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kythnos/#dryopida-panigiri-of-agioi-apostoloi-dryopida
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kythnos/#dryopida-panigiri-of-agioi-apostoloi-dryopida
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:meganisi-katomeri-panigiri-of-agioi-apostoloi-katomeri-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270628
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270630
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agioi Apostoloi\, Katomeri
LOCATION:Katomeri\, Meganisi\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Katomeri's parish church is dedicated to Peter and Paul and its feast on 29 June is the first panigiri of the Meganisi summer: vespers on the 28th\, liturgy and then food and music in the village square. Small island\, small crowd\, mostly locals and yacht crews from Vathy and Spartochori.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/meganisi/#katomeri-panigiri-of-agioi-apostoloi-katomeri
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/meganisi/#katomeri-panigiri-of-agioi-apostoloi-katomeri
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:paxos-gaios-panigiri-of-agioi-apostoloi-gaios-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270628
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270630
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agioi Apostoloi\, Gaios
LOCATION:Gaios\, Paxos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The Corfu-region festival calendars list Gaios among the places keeping Peter and Paul on 29 June\, with vespers on the 28th and a village evening with music and food on the square\; Paxos also joins Corfu in the Panagia Vlachernon celebrations on 2 July. Small and local\; ask at the port kiosk which square the music is in.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/paxos/#gaios-panigiri-of-agioi-apostoloi-gaios
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/paxos/#gaios-panigiri-of-agioi-apostoloi-gaios
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:serifos-platys-gialos-panigiri-of-agioi-apostoloi-platys-gialos-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270628
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270630
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agioi Apostoloi\, Platys Gialos
LOCATION:Platys Gialos\, Serifos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The first big feast of the Serifos summer\, at the chapel of Peter and Paul by the beach of Platys Gialos in the north: vespers on the evening of 28 June\, a communal meal put on by the ktitores (the families who keep the church) — fava\, goat with pasta\, local wine — then liturgy and more food next morning. The road from Chora is partly unpaved and the bay has no lighting\, so drive carefully and bring a torch.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/serifos/#platys-gialos-panigiri-of-agioi-apostoloi-platys-gialos
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/serifos/#platys-gialos-panigiri-of-agioi-apostoloi-platys-gialos
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ikaria-pezi-panigiri-of-the-twelve-apostles-pezi-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270629
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270701
SUMMARY:Panigiri of the Twelve Apostles\, Pezi
LOCATION:Pezi\, Ikaria\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Pezi is the high\, wind-blown plateau village above Raches\, and its Agioi Apostoloi feast on the evening of 29 June is the first proper panigiri of the summer in the west of the island. Goat\, local wine and a violin-and-laouto orchestra in the square\; bring a jacket\, it is cold up there even in June. Nearby Agios Isidoros (Pezi) has its own small feast on 14 May.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#pezi-panigiri-of-the-twelve-apostles-pezi
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#pezi-panigiri-of-the-twelve-apostles-pezi
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kos-antimachia-panigiri-of-agioi-apostoloi-antimachia-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270629
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270701
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agioi Apostoloi\, Antimachia
LOCATION:Antimachia\, Kos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Antimachia\, the big windmill village in the middle of the island\, has its patronal feast for the Holy Apostles on 29-30 June\, with vespers and a glendi with local music and food on the square. The same village feasts the Panagia on 15 August and runs the honey festival in August.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kos/#antimachia-panigiri-of-agioi-apostoloi-antimachia
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kos/#antimachia-panigiri-of-agioi-apostoloi-antimachia
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:naxos-melanes-panigiri-of-agioi-apostoloi-melanes-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270629
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270701
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agioi Apostoloi\, Melanes
LOCATION:Melanes\, Naxos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Melanes\, the village of the kouroi near Chora\, celebrates the Holy Apostles on the evening of 29 June with a panigiri in the square: local meat dishes\, wine and violin-and-laouto dancing. One of the first big feasts of the Naxos summer and an easy 15-minute drive from town.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/naxos/#melanes-panigiri-of-agioi-apostoloi-melanes
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/naxos/#melanes-panigiri-of-agioi-apostoloi-melanes
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:agistri-skala-panigiri-of-agioi-anargyroi-skala-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270630
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270702
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agioi Anargyroi\, Skala
LOCATION:Skala\, Agistri\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The blue-domed church above Skala beach is Agioi Anargyroi\, and its feast on 1 July (vespers on the 30th) is the main panigiri of the port village\, with food and music by the church after the service. Agistri is 20 minutes from Aegina by boat\, so it is easy to combine with a day on the beach.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/agistri/#skala-panigiri-of-agioi-anargyroi-skala
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/agistri/#skala-panigiri-of-agioi-anargyroi-skala
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:amorgos-tholaria-panigiri-of-agioi-anargyroi-tholaria-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270630
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270702
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agioi Anargyroi\, Tholaria
LOCATION:Tholaria\, Amorgos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Tholaria above Aegiali celebrates its parish saints on 30 June-1 July: great vespers on the eve\, liturgy and procession of the icons on the day\, and both evenings the whole village eats patatato (goat with potatoes) and xydato (sour meat soup) in the square and dances to violin and laouto. Vegetarian dishes replace the meat if the feast falls on a fasting day. Stay in Aegiali and walk or take the shuttle up.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/amorgos/#tholaria-panigiri-of-agioi-anargyroi-tholaria
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/amorgos/#tholaria-panigiri-of-agioi-anargyroi-tholaria
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ikaria-karavostamo-panigiri-of-agioi-anargyroi-karavostamo-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270630
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270702
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agioi Anargyroi\, Karavostamo
LOCATION:Karavostamo\, Ikaria\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Karavostamo\, the big seaside village between Evdilos and Agios Kirykos\, opens its summer with Agioi Anargyroi on the evening of 30 June\; the same village does Agia Paraskevi (25 July) and the huge 15 August feast\, so it is the busiest panigiri village on the north coast. Food is served at long tables by the cultural association\, music is Ikarian violin. Therma on the south coast celebrates the same saints the same night.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#karavostamo-panigiri-of-agioi-anargyroi-karavostamo
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#karavostamo-panigiri-of-agioi-anargyroi-karavostamo
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ithaca-frikes-panigiri-of-agioi-apostoloi-frikes-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270630
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270701
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agioi Apostoloi\, Frikes
LOCATION:Frikes\, Ithaca\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The first panigiri of the Ithacan summer\, on the little harbour of Frikes for Peter and Paul: liturgy\, then tables on the quay with grilled meat\, local wine and a live band until morning. Half the crowd comes off the yachts moored a few metres away\, so it is more cosmopolitan than most\; the municipality lists it for 30 June\, and Frikes also throws a second summer party around 10 August.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ithaca/#frikes-panigiri-of-agioi-apostoloi-frikes
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ithaca/#frikes-panigiri-of-agioi-apostoloi-frikes
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kythnos-dryopida-panigiri-of-agioi-anargyroi-at-the-katafyki-cave-dr-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270630
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270702
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agioi Anargyroi at the Katafyki cave\, Dryopida
LOCATION:Dryopida\, Kythnos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Kythnos has four Agioi Anargyroi chapels celebrating on 1 July\, but the memorable one is at Dryopida\, where the chapel sits at the mouth of the Katafyki cave that villagers once used as a refuge. Vespers on the evening of 30 June is followed by a glenti with violin and laouto\; it comes two days after the Apostoloi feast\, so a late-June stay in Dryopida catches both.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kythnos/#dryopida-panigiri-of-agioi-anargyroi-at-the-katafyki-cave-dr
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kythnos/#dryopida-panigiri-of-agioi-anargyroi-at-the-katafyki-cave-dr
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:salamis-selinia-feast-of-panagia-therapevousa-agios-nikolaos-selinia-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270630
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270702
SUMMARY:Feast of Panagia Therapevousa\, Agios Nikolaos\, Selinia
LOCATION:Selinia\, Salamina\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The seaside parish of Agios Nikolaos in Selinia\, on the east coast facing Piraeus\, keeps the feast of its icon of Panagia Therapevousa (the Healer) on 30 June-1 July: vespers with artoklasia at 7 pm on the eve\, liturgy at 7 am and a procession of the icon along the waterfront. The same church holds a relic of St Nicholas and celebrates again on 5-6 December.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/salamis/#selinia-feast-of-panagia-therapevousa-agios-nikolaos-selinia
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/salamis/#selinia-feast-of-panagia-therapevousa-agios-nikolaos-selinia
END:VEVENT
